 "new_string": "This recurrence does not resolve the previously unsolved mixed-pair 25×6 case: preserve that separate selector uncertainty. Re-detect every same-color diagonal adjacent pair in a fresh input, project each outward ray from its endpoints, and mechanically validate exact dimensions and blockers before submitting.\n\n### Accepted recurrence: task-7c19c728, diagonal pairs with directional blockers (23×21)\n\nA fresh test was accepted first try after one demo. Background 4; preserve all non-background input cells and extend each diagonal same-color adjacent pair outward along its diagonal through background cells only, stopping at the first occupied cell or edge. Demo (16×25, background 7): the diagonal 8 pair `(12,18),(13,17)` had a horizontal extra 8 at `(12,19)`; the outward NW-side ray was blocked immediately by 2 at `(11,19)`, while the other side extended from `(13,17)` down-left through `(14,16),(15,15)` to the edge. Isolated 4 at `(11,18)` and 2 at `(11,19)` remained unchanged. Accepted test pairs (zero-based): 9s at `(15,11),(16,10)` and 2s at `(15,12),(16,13)`. The 9 pair extended from `(16,10)` down-left through `(17,9),(18,8),(19,7),(20,6),(21,5),(22,4)`; its opposite direction was blocked by 5 at `(14,12)`. The 2 pair extended from `(16,13)` down-right through `(17,14),(18,15),(19,16),(20,17),(21,18),(22,19)`; its opposite direction was blocked by 5 at `(14,11)`. This supports treating any occupied color as a blocker, with the two ends tested independently; extra orthogonal contact does not itself continue the diagonal. Preserve blockers and validate exact bounds before submission."
